# Architecture (Mandatory)

Every change MUST follow layered MVC. Never skip layers or mix responsibilities.

## Layer map

| Layer | Backend | Frontend |
|-------|---------|----------|
| Route | `routes/*.php` | Inertia page name in route |
| Controller | `app/Http/Controllers/` | — |
| Request / Validation | `app/Http/Requests/` | Form validation + server rules |
| Service / Action | `app/Services/` or `app/Actions/` | — |
| Model | `app/Models/` | — |
| View | `resources/js/pages/` | Page components only |
| UI Component | — | `resources/js/components/` |
| Shared logic | `app/Concerns/` | `resources/js/hooks/`, `resources/js/lib/` |

## MVC flow (this project)

```
Route → Controller → (Request) → Service/Action → Model → Inertia::render(page)
                                                              ↓
                                                         Page (View) → Components
```

## Rules

- Controllers: HTTP only — authorize, delegate, return response. Max ~15 lines per action.
- Business logic: ONLY in Services or Actions, never in Controllers or Models.
- Models: Eloquent relations, casts, scopes, fillable. No HTTP or UI logic.
- Pages: compose UI; no direct DB or business rules.
- One feature = one vertical slice across layers (route → controller → service → model → page).

## Before merging

- [ ] No business logic in Controller or Page
- [ ] Validation in Form Request (backend) or dedicated validator
- [ ] New domain logic has a Service/Action class
- [ ] Brand colors rule still respected (`brand-colors.mdc`)
